Date: Wed, 1 Apr 2026 15:02:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] AOSCOS: video: use DRM panel orientation for automatic
 display rotation

- In drm_shared.c, read the DRM connector's "panel orientation" property
  and map its "Right Side Up"/"Upside Down"/"Left Side Up" enumerations
  to 90/180/270 degree clockwise rotations. The result is stored as the
  display's default orientation and exposed through the new
  display_get_default_orientation() accessor.
- Change the default value of the --rotate/rotate configuration option
  from 'normal' to 'auto'. When creating the text renderer for a new
  display, 'auto' resolves the rotation string from the first screen's
  current orientation, or from the DRM panel orientation for the first
  display.
- Tag pointer events with an is_touchscreen flag and, in
  terminal.c's pointer_event(), apply the inverse coordinate
  transformation to absolute touchscreen events and adjust the pointer
  maxima to the last valid coordinate, so that touch input stays aligned
  with the rotated logical display.
- Update the man pages and --help output to document the new 'auto'
  rotation mode.

